                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game sucks IMHO, but it's just one indie developer doing some seriously heavy lifting, so thumbs up.\n\nMy criticisms are directly opposite of the positive reviews.  I find the game to be a bland faux-cyber graphic style.  Other than seeing the gorgeous C64, I just didn't feel that retro, \"boomer shooter\" vibe.  In all honesty it feels very AI assisted, even though I'd imagine it's roots were in a personal project by the developer.  AI is in fact the crux of the games plot, and perhaps that really suits it.\n\nThe audio is near impossible for me to stomach.\n\nThe graphics are over bright and over bloomed, and the polyhedron shaped models feel exactly like...shapes.  The reticle in VR is enormous, and the zoom feature is beyond useless.  It's an audio/visual nightmare, harkening back to those \"design is my passion\" memes.\n\nTo prospective buyers... take your inspiration to buy from the other positive reviews.",
